# Overslept in Russian: проспал, заснул, дочитал
subtitle: "Проспал, заснул, дочитал: how про-, за-, до-, по- and пере- change a verb that has nothing to do with motion."
tags: ["russian","russian prefixes","проспать","russian verbs","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/verb-prefixes","grammar/aspect"]
thumb: "band \"Overslept in Russian\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Dates in Russian history: в 1703 году, в XVIII веке","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/155-russian-history-dates.cast"}

## Overslept in Russian: проспал, заснул, дочитал
